Number of moles
$\begin{aligned}
& =\frac{\text { Mass of a substance }}{\text { Molar mass of the substance }} \\
& =\frac{6.9 \times 10^{-2} \times 1000 \mathrm{~g}}{23 \mathrm{~g} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}=3 \mathrm{moles}
\end{aligned}$

Mass of $6.022 \times 10^{23}$ molecules of water $=1.8 \mathrm{~g}\therefore \quad$ Mass of 1 molecule of water
$\begin{aligned}
& =\frac{18 \mathrm{~g} \times 1}{6.022 \times 10^{23}}=2.98 \times 10^{-23} \mathrm{~g} \\
& \text { Density }=\frac{\text { mass }}{\text { volume }}
\end{aligned}\therefore \quad$ Volume occupied by 1 molecule of water
$=\frac{\text { mass }}{\text { density }}=\frac{2.98 \times 10^{-23} \mathrm{~g}}{1 \mathrm{~g} \mathrm{~cm}^{-3}}=2.98 \times 10^{-23} \mathrm{~cm}^3$

